abstract: "Dirichlet Weight Regularization (dreg) — a discrete 2D Dirichlet harmonic energy penalty that breaks permutation symmetry, concentrates 2D-DCT spectral energy, and improves hierarchical Base-3 trit spectral quantization (.tritq) across a configurable 0.43–3.77 bpp rate-distortion frontier. Validated on TinyStories-10M (72.1% roughness reduction; 6.76–7.25 PPL gain at calibrated 1.638 bpp and 7.02 PPL gain at 2.181 bpp) and MNIST MLPs (-84.5% roughness; +10.72% low-pass truncation accuracy), paired with a portable C11 zero-copy DMA micro-kernel."
